{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal model using weighted fusion instead of no aggregation, comparing it to the concat fusion baseline (experiment 002). The weighted fusion achieved 52.3% validation accuracy (vs. 52.66% for concat) and 50.8% F1, suggesting no significant improvement from the more sophisticated fusion strategy. The result indicates uncertainty about whether weighted fusion provides benefits over simple concatenation, as the similar performance lacks direct comparative evidence isolating the fusion method's impact."
}

